{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"Dimension table (mm; angles in degrees):\n\n| Feature | Printed values |\n|---|---|\n| Main housing | Ø170 inner opening; Ø195 mounting bolt circle |\n| Main mounting holes | 8 × Ø10 through; paired positions at 30° and 60° in each quadrant |\n| Web openings | 7 × Ø27.5 through on Ø130; 36° spacing, starting 18° below horizontal |\n| Central stepped bore | Ø50 through, Ø60 recesses; 84.3-wide central section plateau |\n| Section B–B | 45 from front rim to web/wall junction; 34 from front rim to side-hole axis; 16 recess span; 16.1 outer tab extension; 11 side-hole depth; 81.3 to the web transition; 157.5° taper |\n| Top neck | Ø65 opening, Ø75 bolt circle; 6 × Ø7 at 60°; R7.5 lugs, R10 blends |\n| Neck internal detail | Ø27 passage, Ø35 surrounding boss; 8-wide web; R35 relief |\n| Sloping mounting faces | 4 × Ø10 per face, 60 × 25 spacing; slot with R12.5 ends and 20 centre spacing; slot offset 2.5; wall 10 |\n| Ribs and tabs | 5-wide ribs; 22 inner tab length; 18°/36° radial layout |\n| Other profile callouts | 107.6 and 106.3 typical; 45° face orientation; R1.5, R2.5, R3, R5, R7 |\n\nI’m taking the front rim as axial zero. The 45 and 34 dimensions both begin at that rim and end respectively at the web junction and side-hole axis, so neither is an added thickness. The recess chain is `front hub face = 45 − 16 = 29`. Across the housing, `tab outside span = 170 + 2×16.1 = 202.2`; the 11 dimension ends at the blind-hole bottom, not the inner wall.\n\nThe total axial depth and neck height are not explicitly dimensioned. I’ll use 100 overall axial depth and a 25 neck extension, preserving the symmetric section form. Those are assumptions rather than printed dimensions.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"build123d","tool":"execute","arguments":{"code":"from build123d import *\nimport math\ninner_dia = 170.0 # mm\nbolt_pcd = 195.0 # mm\nmount_dia = 10.0 # mm\nmount_count = 8\nwindow_dia = 27.5 # mm\nwindow_pcd = 130.0 # mm\nwindow_count = 7\nwindow_pitch = 36.0 # deg\nwindow_start = -18.0 # deg\nbore_dia = 50.0 # mm\ncounterbore_dia = 60.0 # mm\nplateau_dia = 84.3 # mm\njunction_depth = 45.0 # mm overall from front rim\nside_axis_depth = 34.0 # mm overall from front rim\nrecess_depth = 16.0 # mm component\ntab_extension = 16.1 # mm component beyond cavity\nside_hole_depth = 11.0 # mm component\ntransition_radius = 81.3 # mm\ntaper_angle = 157.5 # deg\nneck_bore = 65.0 # mm\nneck_pcd = 75.0 # mm\nneck_hole_dia = 7.0 # mm\nneck_hole_count = 6\nneck_pitch = 60.0 # deg\nneck_lug_r = 7.5 # mm\nneck_blend_r = 10.0 # mm\npassage_dia = 27.0 # mm\npassage_boss_dia = 35.0 # mm\nneck_web_width = 8.0 # mm\nrelief_radius = 35.0 # mm\nside_spacing = 60.0 # mm\nside_row_spacing = 25.0 # mm\nslot_end_r = 12.5 # mm\nslot_centres = 20.0 # mm\nslot_offset = 2.5 # mm\nslant_wall = 10.0 # mm\nrib_width = 5.0 # mm\ntab_inner_length = 22.0 # mm\nexternal_typ = 107.6 # mm\ninternal_typ = 106.3 # mm\nhub_radial_ref = 42.1 # mm\nface_angle = 45.0 # deg\nlug_radius = 7.0 # mm\nouter_fillet = 1.5 # mm\ninternal_fillet = 2.5 # mm\ntab_fillet = 5.0 # mm\ntransition_fillet = 3.0 # mm\naxial_depth = 100.0 # mm assumed undimensioned overall\nneck_extension = 25.0 # mm assumed undimensioned\nshell_wall = 11.0 # mm inferred from rear wall / tab inner bore dimension\nweb_min_thickness = 8.0 # mm inferred central neck web\nrib_relief = 5.0 # mm assumed raised cast ribs\nneck_wall = 5.0 # mm inferred (75-65)/2\noverlap = 1.0 # mm construction overlap\nzero = 0.0 # mm datum\nfull_turn = 360.0 # deg\nhalf_turn = 180.0 # deg\nright_angle = 90.0 # deg\nmount_angle_a = 30.0 # deg\nmount_angle_b = 60.0 # deg\nri = inner_dia/2\nro = ri+shell_wall\nhalf_depth = axial_depth/2\nhub_front = junction_depth-recess_depth\nhub_back = axial_depth-hub_front\nweb_front = half_depth-web_min_thickness/2\nweb_back = half_depth+web_min_thickness/2\n# Main axis Z. Front elevation is XY; neck points +Y.\n# Revolved shell, tapered web and central stepped bore.\nprofile_points = [(ri,zero),(ro,zero),(ro,axial_depth),(ri,axial_depth),\n (ri,web_back),(plateau_dia/2,hub_back),(counterbore_dia/2,hub_back),\n (counterbore_dia/2,axial_depth-junction_depth),(bore_dia/2,axial_depth-junction_depth),\n (bore_dia/2,junction_depth),(counterbore_dia/2,junction_depth),\n (counterbore_dia/2,hub_front),(plateau_dia/2,hub_front),(ri,web_front)]\nwith BuildPart() as core:\n with BuildSketch(Plane.XZ):\n  Polygon(*profile_points,align=None)\n revolve(axis=Axis.Z)\npart = core.part\n# Broad angled mounting pads join the annular casting; bounded by the octagonal roof.\npad_normal = bolt_pcd/2\npad_width = side_spacing+2*mount_dia\nfor sign in [-1,1]:\n a=sign*face_angle\n pad=Pos(zero,pad_normal-slant_wall/2,half_depth)*Box(pad_width,slant_wall,axial_depth)\n pad=Rot(Z=-a)*pad\n part=part.fuse(pad)\n# main mounting ears\nmount_angles=[mount_angle_a,mount_angle_b,half_turn-mount_angle_b,half_turn-mount_angle_a,\n half_turn+mount_angle_a,half_turn+mount_angle_b,full_turn-mount_angle_b,full_turn-mount_angle_a]\nfor a in mount_angles:\n x=bolt_pcd/2*math.cos(math.radians(a)); y=bolt_pcd/2*math.sin(math.radians(a))\n part=part.fuse(Pos(x,y,half_depth)*Cylinder(lug_radius+internal_fillet,axial_depth))\n# Flat lower foot connecting lower paired ears.\nfoot_y=-(bolt_pcd/2*math.sin(math.radians(mount_angle_b))+lug_radius)\nfoot_width=bolt_pcd*math.cos(math.radians(mount_angle_b))\npart=part.fuse(Pos(zero,foot_y+shell_wall/2,half_depth)*Box(foot_width,shell_wall,axial_depth))\n# Reopen the large cavities, leaving the taper and central web.\nwith BuildPart() as front_void:\n with BuildSketch(Plane.XZ):\n  Polygon((zero,-overlap),(ri,-overlap),(ri,web_front),(plateau_dia/2,hub_front),(zero,hub_front),align=None)\n revolve(axis=Axis.Z)\npart=part.cut(front_void.part)\npart=part.cut(Pos(zero,zero,axial_depth)*mirror(front_void.part,about=Plane.XY))\nshow(part,\"housing\")\n"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
